From 99924ed6f0f1622f561f684959fc61666602b236 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Intel MPSS <mpss@intel.invalid>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 09:57:33 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 08/16] x86/mic: KNC APIC, IOAPIC and SMP bringup

From Intel MPSS 3.8.6:
 - The 9-bit APIC id lives in LAPIC ID bits 31:23 (apicdef.h,
   physflat get/set_apic_id, the AP id extraction in head_64.S);
   recalibrate_lapic() for cpufreq changes; no C3STOP on the LAPIC
   timer.
 - IOAPIC: memory-mapped register access through mic_def.h, a 64-bit
   IOAPIC address (unsigned long apicaddr, u64 mp_register_ioapic:
   KNC's IOAPIC sits above 4G at 0x08007DA800), 25 pins, and the KNC
   route-entry layout (destination id in bits 32-39).
 - smpboot: BSP hooks (icache snoop off, SMPT init) and the KNC IOAPIC
   pin table.

Adaptations for 6.18:
 - 6.5 parallel bringup: the AP reads its APIC id from the LAPIC and
   took bits 31:24; on KNC every AP looked up the wrong CPU ("APIC id
   mismatch") and the boot timed out. Bits 31:23 on EARLYMIC; all 240
   CPUs come up with x86_cpuinit.parallel_bringup at its default.
 - 5.11's ioapic_setup_msg_from_msi() writes the destination through
   the IR index overlay (bits 56-63); the KNC IOAPIC keeps it in bits
   32-39, so every IOAPIC interrupt targeted APIC 0 with a vector
   allocated elsewhere. destid_0_7/virt_destid_8_14 are copied by
   name on EARLYMIC; IO_APIC_route_entry is a union since 5.15.
 - 4.15's vector domain assigns on activation, spreading vectors over
   CPUs; the SBOX ICR has one fixed destination, so the doorbell irqs
   are allocated with mask cpumask_of(0) and program cfg->dest_apicid.
 - 3.17 sizes the irqdomain and pin_info from the GSI range: 25 pins
   for both; mp_register_ioapic() keeps the u64 address (3.17 took
   u32 back and truncated it: fixmap on RAM at 0x7DA800, heap
   corruption). The mp_irqs pin table is filled right after the SFI
   IOAPIC registration (setup_IO_APIC runs from late_time_init).
 - 6.9 topology rework: only physflat remains; the old
   generic_processor_info()/physid_mask_t users are gone.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Anselm Busse <anselm.busse@outlook.com>
